apply_instruction:
Application Procedure:

Interested and eligible candidates are requested to submit:

A detailed and updated Curriculum Vitae (CV);
A cover letter expressing interest in the position;
Copies of academic certificates and transcripts;
Details of teaching, research and administrative experience;
List of publications and major research achievements;
A brief Vision/Strategic Plan for the Development of SMUCT; and
Names and contact details of three professional referees.

Applications should be submitted on or before 31st October 2026 in a sealed envelope marked "Application for the Post of Vice-Chancellor" or by email to:

The Chairman, Board of Trustees
Shanto-Mariam University of Creative Technology Trust
Plot-06, Road/Avenue-06, Sector-17/H-1, Uttara, Dhaka-1230

Email: chairman_bot@smuct.ac.bd
www.smuct.ac.bd
